 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Projective space is proper over its base",
 "statement": "For every finite index set $n$ and every scheme $S$, the structural\nmorphism $\\mathbf P(n;S)\\to S$ is proper.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-lem-nagata-sketch-affine-cover/lemma-nagata-projective-space-base-change-proper.md",
  "place": "node lemma-nagata-projective-space-base-change-proper, order 308"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-nagata-projective-space-base-change"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The polynomial ring $\\mathbf Z[T_i:i\\in n]$ is of finite type over the\ndegree-zero part of its total-degree grading, which is $\\mathbf Z$, because\n$n$ is finite. Hence the verified properness instance for\n$\\operatorname{Proj}$ of a graded ring of finite type over its degree-zero\npart ([def-nagata-affine-proj]) makes\n$\\mathbf P^n_{\\mathbf Z}\\to\\operatorname{Spec}\\mathbf Z$ proper. Since\n$\\operatorname{Spec}\\mathbf Z$ is the terminal scheme, the same holds for\n$\\mathbf P^n_{\\mathbf Z}\\to\\ast$, and properness is stable under base\nchange, so the first projection $\\mathbf P(n;S)\\to S$ is proper.",
   "uses": [
    "def-nagata-affine-proj"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
